<attribute name="mainDescription" nodeId="cc0db36a">&lt;p&gt;
    Establish the project baseline with the project management plan (PMP). Review and obtain approval of the project
    management plan (PMP) document. Once approved, the PMP will serve as the project baseline against which the project
    will be measured to remain on track and in control.&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;</attribute>
<attribute name="externalId" nodeId="f6a8f765"></attribute>
<attribute name="keyConsiderations" nodeId="363a88f2">Project baselines can be done for schedule, cost and scope. These baselines are often combined to develop a performance
measurement baseline that is used as an overall project baseline for earned value measurements. However, most small
projects should only need one baseline (e.g., schedule) to track against. &lt;br /&gt;</attribute>
<attribute name="longPresentationName" nodeId="d4146e78"></attribute>
<attribute name="purpose" nodeId="7856ed0e">&lt;p&gt;
    To define a beginning for project progress tracking and control.
&lt;/p&gt;</attribute>
